"<div><div class=\" response-message\"></div></div><h2>Progression System Design</h2>\n<p>✅ Design complete</p>\n<p>This progression system is designed for <strong>Galactic Trader</strong>, a strategy game where players manage a fleet, craft advanced components, and optimize resource chains. Despite the title, per the design constraints, &quot;Trading&quot; is replaced by <strong>Contract Fulfillment</strong> (a crafting-based delivery system) to maintain the strategy focus without a player-to-player market.</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>1. The Four-Resource Economy (Foundation)</h3>\n<p>To understand progression, we must define the resources being managed:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Galactic Credits (Currency):</strong> Earned via contracts; used for facility maintenance and blueprint purchases.</li>\n<li><strong>Asteroid Ore (Basic Material):</strong> Harvested from belts; the primary ingredient for early-game crafting.</li>\n<li><strong>Isotope Shards (Advanced Material):</strong> Found in hazardous zones; required for high-tier tech and engine upgrades.</li>\n<li><strong>Data Slates (Experience/Research):</strong> Generated through exploration and successful crafting; the primary source of XP.</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<h3>2. Linear Experience Curve</h3>\n<p>The progression follows a <strong>Linear Growth Model</strong>, where the XP required for the next level increases by a fixed increment. This ensures that while the game gets harder, the goals remain predictable and reachable.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Base XP for Level 1:</strong> 1,000 XP</li>\n<li><strong>Increment per Level:</strong> +1,000 XP</li>\n<li><strong>Formula:</strong> $XP\\ to\\ Level\\ (N) = N \\times 1,000$</li>\n<li><strong>Total XP to Max Level (30):</strong> 465,000 XP</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th align=\"left\">Tier</th><th align=\"left\">Levels</th><th align=\"left\">XP per Level</th><th align=\"left\">Total Tier XP</th><th align=\"left\">Estimated Time</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Early Game</strong></td><td align=\"left\">1–10</td><td align=\"left\">1k – 10k</td><td align=\"left\">55,000</td><td align=\"left\">5–8 Hours</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Mid Game</strong></td><td align=\"left\">11–20</td><td align=\"left\">11k – 20k</td><td align=\"left\">155,000</td><td align=\"left\">20–25 Hours</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Late Game</strong></td><td align=\"left\">21–30</td><td align=\"left\">21k – 30k</td><td align=\"left\">255,000</td><td align=\"left\">35–45 Hours</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Total</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>30</strong></td><td align=\"left\">--</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>465,000</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>~60–80 Hours</strong></td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h3>3. Unlock Schedule &amp; Milestones</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th align=\"left\">Level</th><th align=\"left\">Unlock Category</th><th align=\"left\">Description</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>1</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Basics</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Starter Ship (The &quot;Mule&quot;), Ore Refiner, Tier 1 Contracts.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>5</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Automation</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Auto-Miner Drone (reduces manual clicking for Ore).</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>10</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Milestone 1</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>The Frigate Class:</strong> Unlocks multi-slot ships and Isotope Shard harvesting.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>15</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Crafting</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Chemical Lab: Allows crafting of &quot;Hyper-Fuel&quot; from Isotope Shards.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>20</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Milestone 2</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>The Industrial Rig:</strong> Massive storage capacity; unlocks &quot;Deep Space&quot; sectors.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>25</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Advanced Tech</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Matter Reconstructor: Converts Ore directly into Tech-Scrap at a high cost.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>30</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Milestone 3</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><strong>The Galactic Command:</strong> Final ship; unlocks &quot;Endless Contracts&quot; and Prestige.</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h3>4. Skill Trees (The &quot;Specialization&quot; System)</h3>\n<p>Players earn <strong>1 Skill Point per level</strong> (30 total). There are 3 branches, each with 10 skills.</p>\n<h4><strong>Branch A: The Industrialist (Crafting &amp; Efficiency)</strong></h4>\n<p><em>Focus: Reducing resource costs and increasing output.</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Waste Not:</strong> 5% chance to not consume Ore when crafting.</li>\n<li><strong>Rapid Assembly:</strong> Crafting timers reduced by 10%.</li>\n<li><strong>Bulk Processing:</strong> Refiners produce 15% more material per cycle.</li>\n<li><strong>Synergy - &quot;Master Smith&quot;:</strong> If Branch B is also at Level 5, unlock &quot;Instant Craft&quot; for Tier 1 items.</li>\n</ol>\n<h4><strong>Branch B: The Navigator (Exploration &amp; Speed)</strong></h4>\n<p><em>Focus: Fuel efficiency and reaching new resource nodes faster.</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Light Footprint:</strong> Reduce Fuel-Cell consumption by 10%.</li>\n<li><strong>Engine Overclock:</strong> Travel speed between sectors increased by 15%.</li>\n<li><strong>Sensor Sweep:</strong> 10% higher chance to find rare Isotope Shards.</li>\n<li><strong>Synergy - &quot;Pathfinder&quot;:</strong> If Branch C is also at Level 5, unlock &quot;Warp Jump&quot; (Instant travel to visited sectors).</li>\n</ol>\n<h4><strong>Branch C: The Tycoon (Logistics &amp; Revenue)</strong></h4>\n<p><em>Focus: Maximizing Credit gain and storage.</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Cargo Compression:</strong> Increase ship storage capacity by 20%.</li>\n<li><strong>Contract Negotiation:</strong> Earn 10% more Credits from all deliveries.</li>\n<li><strong>Bulk Discounts:</strong> Blueprint costs in the shop reduced by 15%.</li>\n<li><strong>Synergy - &quot;Market Corner&quot;:</strong> If Branch A is also at Level 5, unlock &quot;Priority Shipping&quot; (Double XP from contracts).</li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<h3>5. Progression Balance &amp; Mechanics</h3>\n<h4><strong>Early Game (Levels 1-10): The Hook</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rhythm:</strong> Rapid-fire unlocks. Every level provides a new blueprint or ship part.</li>\n<li><strong>Goal:</strong> Establish a basic loop: Mine Ore $\\rightarrow$ Craft Components $\\rightarrow$ Complete Contracts $\\rightarrow$ Level Up.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>Mid Game (Levels 11-20): The Optimization</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rhythm:</strong> Progression slows. Players must now manage Isotope Shards (rarer) and Fuel-Cells.</li>\n<li><strong>Goal:</strong> Automate the Ore collection so the player can focus on high-tier crafting and exploring dangerous sectors.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>Late Game (Levels 21-30): The Mastery</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rhythm:</strong> Long-term goals. Levels require significant Data Slate (XP) accumulation.</li>\n<li><strong>Goal:</strong> Building the &quot;Galactic Command&quot; ship. Players must optimize their skill tree synergies to handle the massive resource requirements of end-game blueprints.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>Respec Mechanics</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The &quot;Neural Reset&quot;:</strong> Players can reset their skill tree at any time.</li>\n<li><strong>Cost:</strong> The cost is <strong>10% of current Galactic Credits</strong>. This makes respecs &quot;cheap&quot; for players who have managed their economy poorly (helping them fix it) but &quot;expensive&quot; for wealthy players, preventing them from constantly swapping skills for every single task.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>Casual vs. Hardcore Balance</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Casuals:</strong> Benefit from the <strong>Linear XP curve</strong>. They never feel like they've hit an exponential &quot;wall.&quot; Even 20 minutes of play guarantees progress toward the next level.</li>\n<li><strong>Hardcore:</strong> Benefit from <strong>Skill Synergies</strong>. By carefully balancing points across two trees, hardcore players can unlock &quot;Warp Jumps&quot; or &quot;Instant Crafting,&quot; allowing them to progress through the late-game tiers 2-3x faster than a non-optimized player.</li>\n</ul>\n<div><div class=\" completion-message response-message\"></div></div>"